## COMMON PITFALLS TO AVOID

Quick reminders before submitting. Items overlapping with hard gates note the gate in parentheses; the authoritative definition lives in `Validation Contract`.

- Do not apply patches without committing and moving tags. (verified by `B_state_tags_consistent`)
- Do not forget to verify patches persist across `git checkout`.
- Do not modify files in `{{ repo_path }}` directly.
- Do not skip Phase 0; command and report format depend on framework detection.
- Do not proceed to the next phase before the current phase has a normal test signal.
- Do not add artificial skips to make a result look clean. (caught by `H_s2s_not_above_base` / `H_patched_clean_signal`)
- Do not delete files or use file-level checkout to hide setup failures. (blocked by `B_lint_block_clean::no_delete` / `no_checkout_file`)
- Do not narrow `test_config.json` to make a waiver appear valid.
- Do not run self-checks through `trial_space` or any older copied runner; use the current `python -m {{ test_runner_script }}` command.
- Do not append source declarations whose bodies contain executable logic (apply the attribution test in `patching.md.j2` Boundary rule). Identifier-only edits and load-time-invariant restorations are allowed; anything that answers the test's behavioral question is not. Caught by `B_lint_block_clean::large_src_append`; if a fix needs more than a shim, use a `bound_waiver`.
- Do not replace existing source function bodies to extend behavior. (caught by `B_lint_block_clean::src_function_replaced`; always fails the attribution test in `patching.md.j2`)
- Do not implement framework features yourself in patch code. The benchmark measures milestone src commits, not your implementations. (Kind 2 in `patching.md.j2` Boundary rule)
- Do not modify files whose role is asserting test outcomes — assertions, parametrize data, expected-value tables, skip markers added to satisfy a hard gate. Runner harness scripts and conftest fixtures are HOW-layer regardless of path; role determines layer. (See `patching.md.j2` Boundary rule.)
- Do not add `pytest_collection_modifyitems` skip logic to conftest, or equivalent collection-modifying hooks in other frameworks, that silently drop tests. Hooks that route or organize tests without dropping any are HOW-layer. (See `patching.md.j2`.)
- Do not silently drop tests via `--ignore`, `-k`, `addopts` filters, or package excludes. The same flags are HOW-layer when used to route excluded tests into a separate `test_config.json` mode — document the routing in `unbound_issues.evidence`. (See `patching.md.j2`.)

Positive checks:

- Commit patches with an `[ENV-PATCH]` prefix.
- Test both START and END states after patching.
- Document patched files and the reason for each patch.
- Let the pipeline decide final acceptance through `{{ build_status_path }}`.
